TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` and `[After(…)]` attributes with a `HookType` enum to control scope. Here's a sketch for each:

## 1. Before/After Every Test (method-level)

```csharp
public class MyTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        // Runs before each [Test] in this class
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        // Runs after each [Test] in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public void OrderIsCreated() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Before/After the Class (class-level fixture)

```csharp
public class IntegrationTests
{
    private static HttpClient _client;

    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture()
    {
        // Runs once before the first test in this class
        _client = new HttpClient();
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture()
    {
        // Runs once after the last test in this class
        _client.Dispose();
    }

    [Test]
    public void GetReturnsOk() { /* ... */ }
}
```

> Note: class-level hooks must be **`static`**.

## 3. Before/After the Assembly

```csharp
public static class WireMockSetup
{
    private static WireMockServer _server;

    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartServer()
    {
        // Runs once before any test in this assembly
        _server = WireMockServer.Start();
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopServer()
    {
        // Runs once after all tests in this assembly finish
        _server.Stop();
    }
}
```

> The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it automatically.

## 4. Before/After the Entire Test Session

```csharp
public static class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations()
    {
        // Runs once at the very start of the test run
        await DatabaseHelper.MigrateAsync();
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDown()
    {
        // Runs once at the very end of the test run
        await DatabaseHelper.DropAsync();
    }
}
```

---

## Summary Table

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be | Runs… |
|-------|-----------|----------------|-------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance or static | Around each `[Test]` |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` | Once per test class |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` | Once per assembly |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` | Once for the whole run |

All hooks support `async Task` return types. The `HookType` values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) are imported via `using static TUnit.Core.HookType;`.
